Subject: Re: ATI Rage 128 and UP2000/264DP board
In-Reply-To: <01080713435409.06743@delirium>

On Tue, Aug 07, 2001 at 01:43:54PM -0500, Martin Sanborn wrote:

> 

> However, it appears that it was not installed in a proper slot. When I moved

> it to the PCI slot closed to the edge of the board, it came right up. I was

> under the impression that the "first" slot would be the one closest to the

> processor. Also, it's interesting that while the ATI RagePro-based Xpert 98

> runs fine in any slot, the ATI Rage128-based Xpert 128 will not.

Sounds like a true UP2000, as DP264 has 6 slots, and the one closest

to the edge of the board is PCI peer bus #1, in which a VGA would not

be expected to work.

I believe UP2000 only has one PCI bus, and thus fewer slots (3 or 4,

or is there a bridge?), though a VGA ought to work in any one of

them...

